{title: Goodbye world, goodbye}
{x_theme: heaven, praise}
{x_source: docx:1. Incomplete/Goodbye world goodbye.docx}

{comment: Chorus}
Don’t you weep for me when I’m gone,
For I won’t have the blues anymore
When I hear that last trumpet sound,
My feet won’t stay on the ground
I’m gona rise with a shout I’m gona rise,
I’m gona rise with my Lord to the sky
Heaven is near and I can’t stay here,
Goodbye world, goodbye

{comment: Verse 1}
I told all my troubles goodbye,
Goodbye to each tear and each sigh
This world where I roam cannot be my home,
I’m bound for a land in the sky
I walk and I talk with my Lord,
I feast everyday on His word
Heaven is near and I can’t stay here,
Goodbye world, goodbye

{comment: Verse 2}
I won’t have the blues anymore
When I step across to that shore
I’ll never pine for I’ll leave behind
My heartaches and tears evermore
A day may be two then goodbye,
Tomorrow I’ll rise up and fly
Heaven is near and I can’t stay here,
Goodbye world, goodbye
